"""Measured reader data for a camera-scanning rig (queue M1b, 2026-10-10).

RENDERED SINCE 2026-10-11 (owner decision), ONE RIG ONLY. film_profiles reads
`PER_NEGATIVE_SCANNER_MATRIX_RIG["rgb_led_sony_ilce7rm3"]` and makes it, row-
normalised, the stage-12 `dye_matrix` of the sixteen colour negatives listed
there; the C++ engines receive that matrix through the generated profile
tables, so nothing else here is read at render time. The matrix is DERIVED
from the measured spectra below by
`dye_matrix_from_spectra.per_negative_scanner_rig()`, whose `--assert` pins
the literal. The `rgb_led_mono` rig stays inert (its flat sensor is assumed).

TWO MEASURED INGREDIENTS (owner-approved 2026-10-10; provenance and licence
notices in doc/RESULT_2026-10-10_vision3_mtf_repo_review.md):

  SCANNER_LED_SPD   relative spectral power of ONE measured unit of a
                    narrowband RGB LED light panel (CuteNew RGB Pro Light
                    Source), channels driven alone at 100 % and the white
                    channel at 100 %, 380-780 nm at 1 nm, as measured.
                    Licence CC BY 4.0 (attribution in the RESULT document).
  CAMERA_SSF        relative spectral sensitivity of 44 Bayer cameras,
                    380-780 nm at 5 nm, values verbatim from
                    AcademySoftwareFoundation/rawtoaces-data (Apache-2.0);
                    each entry carries its source URL and SHA-256. Relative
                    scale: only the shape of each curve is meaningful.

WHAT IT IS NOT: a measurement of the owner's own scanner (queue D1 / D2a / D2b
measure that apparatus and stay open), and not a transmission scanner's
manufacturer data. It is a measured reader for a camera + LED rig.
"""

